        <title type="html"><![CDATA[fix(css): clarify atan2() return value documentation]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42308</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42308"/>
        <updated>2025-12-09T05:28:00.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/120158873?u=75bf9ba56f3966c91fa058fa40a362d01ffcd302&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">This PR fixes incorrect wording in the CSS atan2() documentation.</p>
<p dir="auto">The original text incorrectly stated that the function returns “the number of radians representing an angle between -180deg and 180deg”, which mixes units and caused confusion.</p>
<p dir="auto">Updated the sentence to:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Remove the incorrect reference to radians</li>
<li>Clarify that the function returns an angle between -180deg and 180deg, as suggested by the MDN maintainer in issue <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3705588730" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42283" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/42283/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42283">#42283</a>.</li>
</ul>]]></content>
